  "source": {
    "description": "Fixed parse vectors for libsignal v0.99.1 storage records (SessionRecord, PreKeyRecord, SignedPreKeyRecord, KyberPreKeyRecord) and the PQ-ratio session-usability decision. Record bytes come from Java SessionRecordTest (testHasUsablePQRatio, testBadPreKeyRecords); the same prekey-record bytes appear base64-encoded in Swift SessionRecordTests ('CCoSABoA' and 'CCoSABoAIgApAAAAAAAAAAA='). The ratio vectors are the Rust unit test test_should_use_nonpq_session in rust/protocol/src/protocol.rs. Field meanings are in spec/protocol/double-ratchet.md section 10 and spec/protocol/capture.md. 'session_usability' expectations are for the Java call SessionRecord.hasSenderChain(ratio, Instant.EPOCH); the decision logic is in spec/protocol/pqxdh.md section 7 (signal-cli 0.14.7 always uses ratio 0.0). Note that alice_base_key in these synthetic records is 32 raw bytes, not a 33-byte key; only its first 4 bytes are used by the ratio test.",
    "libsignal_repository": "https://github.com/signalapp/libsignal",
    "libsignal_tag": "v0.99.1",
    "libsignal_commit": "97801d22dcf9f5bf714f7b8fa3212cdc973ae1c8",
